            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"validate-the-physics-layer-against-gq39-expert-annotations\">Validate the physics layer against GQ39 expert annotations</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Checks whether the string-length-ratio hui/position model (qinpos.theory) agrees with GQ39's note-by-note (degree, string, position) annotations under the\nplain \"at1\" range convention, with no per-piece gong offset (K)\nor convention correction applied yet?</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This deliberately does NOT do per-piece K/convention fitting or\noutlier repair \u2014 that logic (and the corresponding manual-review\ntables) lives in <code>clean_gq39.py</code>, so it's computed once, not\nduplicated here. This notebook only answers \"is the physics layer\nitself sound\", independent of the cleaning pipeline.</span></span>"
